Reducers rebuild data from an embedding with `inverse_transform(embedding)` when their backend has one, and linear reducers report `reconstruction_error(X)`: the relative squared error `||X - X_hat||^2 / ||X - mean_||^2` on any data, or one value per row with `per_row=True`. On the fit data of PCA it equals `1 - sum(explained_variance_ratio_)`; truncated SVD measures it from the origin.
